1
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,650
Kinetic and potential energy trade places every swing...

2
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,300
...while the total stays flat: energy is conserved.

3
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,250
Add one more joint and the motion becomes chaotic.

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,300
Fully deterministic, yet practically unpredictable.

5
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,450
Three pendulums, started a thousandth of a radian apart.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,300
Within seconds they disagree completely: the butterfly effect.

7
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:37,300
Overrides change model parameters per variant without editing the XML.

8
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:43,300
Coulomb friction: a box slides only when mu < tan(theta).

9
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:46,650
Identical balls; only the contact damping ratio differs.

10
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,300
Lower damping means more energy returned, so a higher bounce.

11
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,450
mjd_transitionFD linearises the dynamics; Riccati gives the gains.

12
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,300
Shove it, and feedback brings it back to balance.

